Authentication and Authorization are two different security concepts.
_________________________________________________________
Authentication is about verifying identity — who the user, service, or application is.
Authorization is about permissions — what actions that identity is allowed to perform on which resources.

In AWS, authentication is handled using IAM, STS, or SSO, while authorization is controlled using IAM policies, resource policies, and SCPs.
In Azure, authentication is done via Azure AD (Entra ID), and authorization is enforced using Azure RBAC roles.

Authentication always happens first; authorization happens after identity is verified.
